Active layers:  L1, L2, L3
Quantum observables are operators (gradient flow generators) on M_QM. Their eigenvalues are the possible measurement outcomes — singulons. The commutator [A,B] measures the non-commutativity of two operators: when [A,B]≠0, the operators' tensor bonds do not commute and the corresponding observables obey a generalized uncertainty null manifold.
Governing law — Canonical commutation relation:  [x,p] = iℏ  ⇒  non-commuting tensor bonds ⇒  Δx·Δp ≥ ℏ/2
The canonical commutation relation is the fundamental null manifold of quantum mechanics. It encodes that position and momentum operators do not commute — their tensor bond is asymmetric — and this asymmetry is precisely the source of the uncertainty principle.

5.4  Quantum Entanglement and Bell's Theorem
M_entangle  Entanglement
Dominant primitives:  T(ψ_A⋕ψ_B) + N(separability) + Attr(Bell-states)
